            <ArticleTitle>Successful epidural anesthesia for cesarean section in a parturient with severe aortic stenosis and a recent history of pulmonary edema--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>142-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 24-year-old 36-week gestation parturient with severe aortic stenosis who developed pulmonary edema during amniocentesis and subsequently underwent a successful cesarean section under epidural anesthesia. Anesthetic management and some pertinent points are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
